# The backend does not reach `str` until the runtime has one. The program is
# CORRECT — that is the whole point of the `unsupported` kind — so the message
# must not invite an edit, and the annotation below is the diagnostic's own
# claim about where it points.
#
# The annotation below sits on the line ABOVE its diagnostic (the next-line form),
# because a binding statement's span runs to the end of its line: with the comment
# on the same line the caret would underline the annotation itself. Queued as a
# span defect.
# Bulk regression case.

function main()
    #~v str
    greeting = "hello"
    print(greeting)
